composed of whole runs, so the run is the unit to which treatment was assigned in both arms.\",\"The selected report demonstrates the issue on its face: it applies a two-sided Fisher exact test to a 2x2 table in which 'each coupon row supplies one observation', yielding n=24 (12 vs 12), while simultaneously stating the 24 rows span only 8 print runs. Fisher's exact test assumes independent observations, but the three coupons from a run share the run's powder lot, recoater condition, gas flow, and thermal history and are explicitly not expected to be independent; the effective number of independent units per arm is 4 runs, not 12 coupons.\",\"The pseudoreplication is material to the stated conclusion: the reported p = 0.0094 comes from treating 24 correlated coupon rows as independent trials. Aggregated at the run level the comparison is 4 nominal runs versus 4 elevated runs, which cannot achieve comparable significance under an exact test, so the row-level p-value overstates the evidence.\",\"No authority lock was minted, so lock conformance is not applicable.\"]}","structured_output":{"declaration_consistent":true,"selected_report_demonstration":"issue","lock_follows_declaration":"not-applicable-no-lock","reasons":["The declared independent-unit column print_run_id is consistent with the frozen data: there are 8 runs (R01-R08) each contributing exactly 3 coupon rows, and laser_setting is constant within every run (R01-R04 all nominal, R05-R08 all elevated), matching the description that the treatment is applied once per run and all build conditions are shared within a run. Both procedure arms (nominal and elevated) are composed of whole runs, so the run is the unit to which treatment was assigned in both arms.","The selected report demonstrates the issue on its face: it applies a two-sided Fisher exact test to a 2x2 table in which 'each coupon row supplies one observation', yielding n=24 (12 vs 12), while simultaneously stating the 24 rows span only 8 print runs. Fisher's exact test assumes independent observations, but the three coupons from a run share the run's powder lot, recoater condition, gas flow, and thermal history and are explicitly not expected to be independent; the effective number of independent units per arm is 4 runs, not 12 coupons.","The pseudoreplication is material to the stated conclusion: the reported p = 0.0094 comes from treating 24 correlated coupon rows as independent trials. Aggregated at the run level the comparison is 4 nominal runs versus 4 elevated runs, which cannot achieve comparable significance under an exact test, so the row-level p-value overstates the evidence.","No authority lock was minted, so lock conformance is not applicable."]},"ttft_ms":6072,"ttft_stream_ms":1562,"time_to_request_ms":11,"type":"result","duration_ms":12783,"uuid":"9778b98a-90cf-47e7-99eb-3b833a1eafab"}
